Parity scope reproduced from the web source:
  - Two data sources: useWatchSummary (GET /watch/summary) load-bearing + useWatchComplication
    (GET /watch/complication) enrichment, combine-latest merged; web isLoading = summaryLoading || compLoading;
    web hasData = summary != null gates the body.
  - Compact (size.cols <= 1, default 1x2): watch-face radial gauge tinted by getBatteryColor (>50 green,
    >20 amber, else red; muted/grey when SoC unknown), StatusBadge(state), converted range, pulsing
    "⚡ Charging" line from complication.charging.
  - Standard (cols >= 2): battery hero big-number + state badge (online->success, asleep->neutral,
    else warning) over a 2-up grid: Range, Lock (Lock/Unlock glyph + badge), Cabin temp, Last Seen.
  - SI display-boundary conversions via shared UnitConverters: range_km (km) x1000 -> m -> display distance;
    inside_temp_c (Celsius) -> display temperature. All numbers 0 decimals (web RadialGauge decimals={0},
    AnimatedNumber default, fmtNumber(_,0)).
  - States: loading / loaded / empty / error / stale / offline (error + empty both render the friendly
    "No watch data" surface; error surfaced via the freshness chip + refresh, faithful to the web shell).
  - i18n: every source key resolves through the P1/S10 facade. All 10 source keys already exist in
    apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw (widget.watchSummary, widget.charging, widget.noWatchData,
    widget.battery, widget.range, widget.lockStatus, widget.locked, widget.unlocked, widget.cabinTemp,
    widget.lastSeen).
  - Accessibility: Narrator names on gauge, state pill, every detail tile, charging line, refresh button;
    reduced-motion honoured (MotionPreference.ReduceMotion); system font scale via tokens.
  - Telemetry: WatchSummaryDiagnostics.RecordViewOpened emits "view.opened slug=WatchSummaryWidget"
    (P1/S11 diagnostics contract), PII-safe.

